# From: https://www.thefreshloaf.com/node/64417/100-sourdough-spelt-bread

starter:
  bread_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter = 20g
  water
  bread_flour
  extra = 0 - starter
  hydration = 100%

dry:
  spelt
  potato_flakes = 4%
  vwg = 4%
  salt = 2%
  yeast = 0.4%

wet:
  cold_water
  leaven = 100g
  old_dough = 100g
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * dry.spelt
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%
  olive_oil = 5%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  # old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough
  hydration = 65%
  total_flour = 400g

/*
4 September 2026

Changes
* My first boule with my new proofing basket
* Guessing at 400g of flour for my 8.5" basket

Next time.
* Remember to remove the old dough!

Day Before
* 20:55, mixed leaven and left on the counter

Baking day

Started at 7:40. Mixed at 8:05, DT=70F. Rest for 30 minutes. Knead
for 3 minutes. It cleaned the bowl.

First rise in the cambro on the counter to 30%.

Shaped and into the basket at 10:50 into the fridge covered with
a shower cap. It was stickier than I expected but a little bench
flour cured that.

I forgot the remove the old dough!

It came easily out of the basket onto the lifter. Placing it into
the preheated cloche went fine.

Baked at 12:25 for 20 minutes at 475F covered and 15 minutes at
425F.

When I removed the lid, the infrared thermometer indicated only
about 400F. More preheat or stop caring.

It looks great for my first try! 3.5 inches tall and 7.25 inches in
diameter.

205F inside.

Looks and tastes great.


*/

